            "review_title": "Review at Limone Italian Foods Cafe & Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Tim L\n38 contributions\n0\nFood was pretty good. Service, not so much.\nDec 2019 • Couples\nWe stopped in for a late lunch/early dinner at around 3PM. Only one table had 2 customers but the 2 waitresses seemed more occupied with whatever they were doing then dealing with customers. We were seated and given menu’s quickly. After about 5 minutes or so of sitting there and not looking at the menu anymore, I had to motion to one of the waitresses to come to the table. She did a couple of other things that she was doing and then came over and took our order. After about 5 minutes or so, she brought our drinks to the table. Then a oil and vinegar, then a minute or so laster, a few slices of cut bread. I would have expected toasted bread from an Italian restaurant but, it wasn’t. Anyway, \nI ordered the lasagne and my gf ordered the spaghetti carbonara. We didn’t have to wait very long for our order, maybe 10/15 minutes which I would expect. The lasagne was pretty good albeit a bit on the dry side as it was lacking in the sauce department. Lots of cheese, meat and fresh noodles though so that part was good. The spaghetti carbonara was very, very good. Actually, I wish that I had ordered that for myself as well instead of the lasagna. After finishing up and waiting for about 10 minutes, I had to motion to the waitress to come to the table and she motioned back asking if I wanted the check, I said no, I wanted to see the dessert menu. She came out from behind the counter with a tray of silverware and dealt with that before bring us the dessert menu. Ordered the tiramisu and a cup of coffee. Tiramisu was quite good, the coffee was a about two inches in the cup. More like a couple of shots of coffee in a regular coffee cup. Needless to say, it was extremely strong. Even after I added milk, I had to add sugar to make it drinkable and I never add sugar to coffee. Overall, a mixed bag of a visit I guess. I probably wouldn’t go back considering the service.\nRead more\nWritten December 18, 2019",
